# Prototype workflow

Read `MEMORY.md` at the start of every session. Never contradict a logged decision without flagging it first. After a significant decision, log: what / why / rejected.

When he says "session end", "wrapping up", or "let's stop here": append a session summary to `MEMORY.md` (worked on / completed / in progress / decisions / next).

If an approach takes more than 2 attempts, log it in `ERRORS.md` and check that file before retrying similar work.

## Research then build — Cursor replacement for Claude.ai / Claude Code

Grok does both. The split exists to keep context debt out of the build, not because the models differ.

1. **Plan chat** — understand the problem, define interaction states, nail design decisions. A quick sketch is fine. A complete TSX artifact here is wasted effort.
2. **Handoff** — before building, write a clean handoff: decisions, component structure, what must not change. Put it in `MEMORY.md` or the first message of a new chat.
3. **Fresh Agent chat** — infrastructure first (App.tsx route, folder, title map). Verify. Then a second scoped prompt for the page itself. One page per prompt.

Start a new thread when the current one is bloated with exploratory back-and-forth.

## Claude conversation import

Recovery, not onboarding. Import only if Jim names a specific in-flight thread. Extract decisions into `MEMORY.md` immediately, then discard the transcript. Do not import a backlog of old chats.

## Page organization

- `src/pages/mobile/[module]/` — mobile (Operate, Assure, Guard, Service)
- `src/pages/operate/` — SmartSense ONE web
- `src/pages/dashboards/` — dashboard prototypes
- `src/pages/user-management/` — existing admin pages

`/mobile/*` gets the minimal shell header. All other routes get the full shell. Already implemented in `src/App.tsx` — do not change that contract.

Do not add a new page to the nav drawer unless the task asks for it.

