## Local review vs share pipeline

Local preview does **not** require a commit. `npm run dev` (Vite) hot-reloads from the working tree. Inspect instantly on localhost. Uncommitted files are visible.

Share pipeline (this repo only — never employer production repos):

1. Edit files locally. Jim reviews on localhost.
2. When a related batch is done, commit it on `main`. Auto-commit is OK after a completed prototype slice. Do not commit after every tiny intermediate edit.
3. Push to `origin` (`https://github.com/jdjensen17-hub/smartsense-prototypes.git`) only when Jim is ready to share. Push updates Vercel project `smartsense-prototypes`.
4. Public URL: `https://smartsense-prototypes.vercel.app` — HashRouter, so share routes as `https://smartsense-prototypes.vercel.app/#/path`.

Do not add a page to the nav drawer just to make it shareable. Do not push the Cursor-setup / calibration diff unless Jim asks.
